      "say": "**None of the three is stable across the two halves.** All three did best in the first half, when AAPL rose about 55 %, and all three lost in the second, when AAPL ended flat.\n\nBy Sharpe: Windows, H1 2.62 > Kagi, H1 1.55 > Renko, H1 −0.73 > Windows, H2 −1.43 > Kagi, H2 −2.75 > Renko, H2 −4.04. By drawdown Kagi fell least in both halves, 8.7 % and 20.4 %, with windows close behind, 9.9 % and 20.6 %.\n\n**Windows** (`docs-demo-gru.keras`) had the best Sharpe in both halves, 2.62 then −1.43, and returned +29.5 % then −13.3 % ([#31 Soft Sirius](https://stage.candlestack.tech/backtests/bt_5usmt72n77), [#32 Fleet Aldebaran](https://stage.candlestack.tech/backtests/bt_r7b4mlpxvw)). **Kagi** (`kagi-trend-smoke.onnx`) came second on Sharpe, 1.55 then −2.75, with +14.0 % then −20.0 % ([#29 Wise Ariel](https://stage.candlestack.tech/backtests/bt_ykv7l2bpyu), [#30 Brave Rhea](https://stage.candlestack.tech/backtests/bt_pmkzny7t5j)). **Renko** (the BLESK model) was last on both measures in both halves, −0.73 then −4.04, with −6.7 % then −28.7 % ([#27 Quick Perseus](https://stage.candlestack.tech/backtests/bt_2osrcfq5se), [#28 Wavy Umbriel](https://stage.candlestack.tech/backtests/bt_7c5leihleb)).\n\nNo run beat buy and hold in the first half. The models were long 58 to 94 % of the time, so their results mostly follow AAPL, and what they add on top of it is small or negative. Buy and hold reads +55.0 % in some runs of the first half and +53.2 % in the windows run, because the runs do not start on the same candle.\n\nLimits: this compares three models, not three representations. Each differs in its architecture and training too, and the Kagi model also in its timeframe, 1h. It is one stock, two half-years and one cost setting, six runs in all, and the Kagi model is a 77-parameter smoke test. To study the representations themselves, train the same network on each of them and run them over more stocks and periods."
